    "title": "pandas.Series.shape — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.shape#\n\n- property Series.shape[source]#\n- Return a tuple of the shape of the underlying data. For a Series this is `(length,)` ; for a 1D Index, likewise a\nsingle-element tuple. Useful for compatibility with NumPy and\nother array-like APIs.See also \n  - `Series.ndim`\n  - Number of dimensions of the underlying data.\n  - `Series.size`\n  - Return the number of elements in the underlying data.\n  - `Series.nbytes`\n  - Return the number of bytes in the underlying data.\n Examples >>> s = pd.Series([1, 2, 3]) >>> s.shape (3,)",
    "markdown_length": 540,
